\begin_layout Section
resolution = flexible
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The goal of this setup is to test the energy balance in time and space.
 To that end,
 the setup starts from resolution = fixed but reduces the resolution of one of the supply units.
 The resolution is only changed at the source such that the supply of the unit is still able to provide the same output as before.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Note Note
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
Flexible time steps can result in conflicting time steps.
 Although perhaps the heuristic of the most overlapping time step could be considered the most logical,
 there are different design decisions.
 Therefore,
 conflicting time steps need to be avoided in the certification process to avoid arbitrary fails.
 Though,
 later on,
 as an extension,
 a setup can be devised where all possible design decisions need to fall within a margin.
 The challenge herein is to ensure that this margin does not allow for other errors to slip in.
 The chance of that happening can be reduced by designing a set of tests that test all the other functionalities first.
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

